{"kind":"assert","text":"Checker Source reconstruction for planner request 78638def (input work spent before the first planned entry), from Main 235e9262. This is arithmetic from Source, not a run or a hosted measurement.\n\nEach exact-object parent read is charged on its maximum, before any I/O, in two places:\n- packages/scope/src/archive-host.ts:97 charges budget.spend({ inputWork: (maximum + 8,192) × 32 + 1,024 }) on v2;\n- packages/git/src/journal-objects.ts:155 (JournalObjectReader.read, boundedObject path) charges inputWork maximum × 4 + 128.\nSo each read costs about 36 × maximum, whatever its actual size.\n\nA reconstruction of the v2 parent reads, with the maxima from journalV2Directory, gives exactly 13 reads. The last is a blob with a 1,048,576-byte maximum, which matches the hosted diagnostic \"ordinal 13, type blob, maximum 1,048,576\":\n1. commit, maximum 1,024: about 0.30 M\n2-3. root and journal/ trees, maximum 295 each: 0.27 M each\n4. journal/v2/, maximum 590: 0.28 M\n5. head.json, maximum 1,024: 0.30 M\n6-10. passes/ and four numeric levels, maximum 4,100 each: 0.41 M each, 2.05 M in all\n11. fifth numeric level, maximum 5,100: 0.45 M\n12. the parent's pass directory, maximum 4,096 × 58 = 237,568: about 8.82 M\n13. the parent's pass manifest blob, maximum JOURNAL_SELECTION_BYTES = 1,048,576: about 38.01 M\nTotal about 50.8 M of the 67,108,864 cap, before planning starts. Reads 12 and 13 alone are about 46.8 M, 70% of the cap, although the real pass.json and directory are a few hundred bytes (524 to 745 tree bytes in total, per 7f1c7d6c). The fixed reservations in archive-build.ts and archive-adaptive.ts (inputWork JOURNAL_SELECTION_BYTES × 3, about 3.1 M each) plausibly make up most of the remaining 9 to 16 M seen in the tails. I have not traced every site.\n\nPossible fix directions, for the builder to weigh (no cap increase):\n(a) Bound reads 12 and 13 by known sizes. If the native receipt or ArchiveRow keeps the parent pass manifest's exact byte length and its directory row count (both are produced natively), those reads can use exact maxima.\n(b) Charge the 32× wire multiplier on the actual framed response, keeping a small fixed pre-I/O reservation. This needs a design decision, because the code deliberately charges before I/O and never refunds.\n(c) Fold this into fc2548ae's bounded native parent-path state, so that a pass reads no old trees or manifests from the host.\nOption (a) looks smallest for the stopgap. A host-shaped witness with a real one-pass parent, asserting the input work spent before planning, would prove it.","body":{"to":"builder"}}